\image(figures/undercomplete_learning.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Fitting losses are measured before minibatch updates; validation losses are measured after each epoch. The curves therefore evaluate different parameter states.)
\alttext(Two measured loss curves over three epochs, with the blue curve reporting fitting loss and the red curve reporting validation loss.)

The fitting pixel mean is the squared-error-optimal constant image. It is a stronger baseline than
black for these sparse handwritten digits. A zero code measures what the decoder bias alone supplies;
cyclically shifting the 200 codes keeps their marginal distribution but destroys alignment with their
own targets. Neither is a newly trained model. Their errors measure dependence on the sample-specific
code, not semantic quality or the usefulness of the code for classification.

Epoch 3 has the lowest validation MSE, 0.04860. Its held-out MSE is 0.05033, about 25.8% below the
fitting-mean baseline's 0.06780. The initial network gives 0.23257, and shifted codes give 0.06821.
Alignment with the input therefore matters, but the short fit still produces visibly blurred digits.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/undercomplete_reconstructions.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::map<std::string, n::Tensor> arrays;
  for (const auto& [name, value] : n::load_npz("build/undercomplete_results.npz"))
    arrays.emplace(name, value);
  const auto input = arrays.at("test_input");
  const auto reconstruction = arrays.at("test_reconstruction");
  const auto labels = arrays.at("test_labels").to_vector<int>();
  std::vector<std::int64_t> rows;
  for (int digit = 0; digit < 10; ++digit) {
    const auto found = std::find(labels.begin(), labels.end(), digit);
    if (found == labels.end()) return 1;
    rows.push_back(found - labels.begin());
  }
  const auto sheet = n::concat({n::take_rows(input, rows), n::take_rows(reconstruction, rows)}, 0).reshape({20, 28, 28, 1});
  n::save_image_grid(sheet, "build/undercomplete_reconstructions.png", 10, 0, 1, 2, 0, 3);
  std::print("Top row: held-out digits 0 through 9, first occurrence of each class. Bottom row: their selected-checkpoint reconstructions.\n");
}
```
